            "showUrl": "/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step2/Electronics/",
            "id": "S3K2QE1M9MSUP13",
            "title": "Electronics",
            "body": "<p>Electrically connect all the components according to the above wiring diagram using <a href=\"https://amzn.to/3Ezn1ao\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">jumper wires<\/a>:<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\"><a href=\"https://amzn.to/4jqEuB1\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ESP32 development board<\/a><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><a href=\"https://amzn.to/4jjZLMN\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">LED Light strip<\/a><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><a href=\"https://www.elationsportstechnologies.com/product-page/single-axis-joystick\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Single-axis joystick<\/a> (center-return style, green color)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://amzn.to/3G1n7I8\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">5VDC Power supply<\/a><\/u><\/li><\/ol><p>For the 5V power supply, use the green screw terminal attachment, and be mindful of the polarity of that connector (power is +, and ground is -) when providing power to the 5V and GND pins on the ESP32 board. Mount the single axis joystick in the level sensing arm slot so that the joystick arm pivots with the sensing arm.<\/p><p>If you would like to change the behavior of the single-axis joystick (spring loaded potentiometer) so that it either returns to its bottom position (black color option), or so that it doesn't have spring-loaded return behavior (orange color option), <a href=\"https://www.elationsportstechnologies.com/product-page/single-axis-joystick\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">variants of the joystick<\/a> are available for purchase. The different variants are useful for different use cases!<\/p>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step2/Electronics/"
        },
        {
            "stepIndex": 3,
            "wordCount": 214,
            "files": [
                {
                    "image": false,
                    "embedType": "NONE",
                    "name": "Pet_Feeder_Level_Sensor.ino",
                    "modifiedDate": "2025-04-22 12:57:35.0",
                    "downloadUrl": "https://content.instructables.com/FNQ/K6WG/M9SIMSJ4/FNQK6WGM9SIMSJ4.ino",
                    "id": "FNQK6WGM9SIMSJ4"
                },
                {
                    "image": true,
                    "embedType": "NONE",
                    "name": "Code.jpg",
                    "modifiedDate": "2025-04-22 12:59:55.0",
                    "width": 861,
                    "mosaic": false,
                    "downloadUrl": "https://content.instructables.com/FRV/A2B7/M9SIMSK6/FRVA2B7M9SIMSK6.jpg",
                    "imageNotes": [],
                    "id": "FRVA2B7M9SIMSK6",
                    "height": 810
                }
            ],
            "showUrl": "/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step3/Code/",
            "id": "SQU02BPM9MSUP18",
            "title": "Code",
            "body": "<p>ESP32 microcontrollers provide extra functionality compared to older Arduino boards, including wireless connectivity, larger memory and higher clock speed. They can be used with the <a href=\"https://www.arduino.cc/en/software/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Arduino IDE<\/a> (Arduino framework) easily. In order to enable ESP32 boards to show up as selectable options in the Arduino IDE software, you can follow the setup procedure in this video made by YouTuber Robonyx:<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/RiYnucfy_rs?si=1MHr4DB6tXuxfL5z&amp;t=124\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">https://youtu.be/RiYnucfy_rs?si=1MHr4DB6tXuxfL5z&amp;t=124<\/a><\/li><\/ol><p>The code uses the Adafruit NeoPixel library for controlling the RGB LEDs - that library can be downloaded using the Arduino IDE. To load the code (Pet_Feeder_Level_Sensor.ino) onto the ESP32 development board, connect the board to your computer using a micro-USB cable, and open the code file in the Arduino IDE. For the board, select \"DOIT ESP32 DEVKIT V1\", and then click Upload to load the code. If the code successfully uploaded, the RGB LED light strip will now react to the joystick position!<\/p><p>If the colors are incorrect (e.g. red, green or yellow when they shouldn't be), remove the joystick + level sensing arm assembly from the dispenser, and turn the power to the ESP32 off and then on again - this will enable the joystick to \"re-zero\" itself so that the center position is calibrated correctly. You can then re-install the joystick and level arm assembly back into the dispenser reservoir.<\/p>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step3/Code/"
        },
        {
            "stepIndex": 4,
            "wordCount": 26,
            "files": [{
                "image": true,
                "embedHtmlCode": "<iframe allowfullscreen=\"\" frameborder=\"0\" height=\"576\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/nUyvoeUkb3w?feature=oembed\" title=\"3D Printable Pet Food Dispenser with ESP32 Level Sensing\" width=\"1024\"><\/iframe>",
                "embedType": "VIDEO",
                "name": "3D Printable Pet Food Dispenser with ESP32 Level Sensing",
                "modifiedDate": "2025-04-22 15:07:06.0",
                "mosaic": false,
                "downloadUrl": "https://content.instructables.com/F74/0P83/M9SIN0AS/F740P83M9SIN0AS.jpg",
                "imageNotes": [],
                "id": "F740P83M9SIN0AS",
                "embedResourceUrl": "https://youtube.com/shorts/nUyvoeUkb3w?feature=share",
                "embedHost": "YouTube",
                "embedAuthor": "Austin Allen"
            }],
            "showUrl": "/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step4/Demonstration/",
            "id": "SGDQMSMM9MSUP19",
            "title": "Demonstration",
            "body": "<p>Here is a demo video showing how the light bar reacts to the level sensor arm, indicating the level of pet food in the reservoir!<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\"><a href=\"https://youtube.com/shorts/nUyvoeUkb3w?feature=share\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">https://youtube.com/shorts/nUyvoeUkb3w?feature=share<\/a><\/li><\/ol>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step4/Demonstration/"
        },
        {
            "stepIndex": 5,
            "wordCount": 193,
            "files": [],
            "showUrl": "/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step5/Conclusion-Next-Steps/",
            "id": "SPG9U6XM9MSUP1A",
            "title": "Conclusion + Next Steps",
            "body": "<p>This project successfully demonstrates:<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\">Reading from a <u><a href=\"https://www.elationsportstechnologies.com/product-page/single-axis-joystick\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">single-axis joystick<\/a><\/u> (spring-loaded potentiometer)<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">Controlling an RGB LED light strip using the Adafruit Neopixel Library<\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\">3D-printing and assembling a custom pet food dispenser<\/li><\/ol><p>To expand on this project, you can utilize the wireless capabilities of the ESP32 microcontroller to enable Bluetooth Low Energy, Wifi, or ESP-NOW communication to transmit the reservoir fill level. The center return single-axis joystick (spring-loaded potentiometer) can also be replaced with one of its variants (bottom return, or no return) to change the behavior of sensing in the assembly. You can also modify the 3D models to adjust the dimensions of the pet feeder if you'd like to change its size or shape.<\/p><p>I hope you enjoyed this project!<\/p><p>Check out my other <u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/member/Penguingineer/instructables/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Instructables articles<\/a><\/u>:<\/p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/ESP32-BaseCam-Bluetooth-Gimbal-Control/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ESP32 + BaseCam Bluetooth Gimbal Control<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/Single-Axis-Joystick-Breakout-Board-Tutorial/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Single-Axis Joystick Controller Module Using Arduino<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/Accuracy-Sensing-Smart-Sports-Rebounder-With-ESP32/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Accuracy-Sensing Smart Sports Rebounder With ESP32<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/EMT-Conduit-Mounted-Weather-Station-Wind-Sensors/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">EMT Conduit-Mounted Weather Station Wind Sensors<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/Telescoping-EMT-Conduit-Pole-Extension-Sensing-Met/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Telescoping EMT Conduit Pole Extension Sensing Methods + Photoresistor Implementation<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/Force-Sensing-Telescoping-EMT-Conduit-Pole/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Force-Sensing Telescoping EMT Conduit Pole<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/Jumbo-Sized-Telescoping-Light-Painter-Made-From-EM/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jumbo-Sized Telescoping Light Painter Made from EMT (Electrical) Conduit<\/a><\/u><\/li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><u><a href=\"https://www.instructables.com/HomemadeDIY-Telescoping-Pole-From-EMT-Electrical-C/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Homemade/DIY Telescoping Pole From EMT (Electrical) Conduit<\/a><\/u><\/li><\/ol><p><br><\/p><p>Thanks for reading!<\/p><p>Austin Allen<\/p><p>Founder and Owner<\/p><p>Elation Sports Technologies LLC<\/p>",
            "url": "https://www.instructables.com/3D-Printable-Pet-Foot-Dispenser-With-Level-Sensing/step5/Conclusion-Next-Steps/"
        }
